{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Restore the staged branch ledger on node1 while retaining the original ledger IDs and amounts.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Node1 contains the staged rows 1001/12.50 and 1002/-3.25, and the final state retains them unchanged alongside the replication test rows.","evidence_ids":["cmd-f0699522a6944d55","cmd-d789f341d5b44e54","cmd-e3da44128e02413c"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Establish node2 as a read-only application replica, with node1 remaining the application writer.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Final configuration shows node1 writable and node2 read-only. A non-administrative account granted INSERT was directly rejected on node2, and both nodes finished with matching ledgers and healthy services.","evidence_ids":["cmd-d7c3971697cc4ad0","cmd-a33a8d47df714d5a","cmd-e3da44128e02413c"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"Use a replication-only account.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Replication uses ledger_repl, restricted to node2's address. Final privilege inspection shows only REPLICATION SLAVE and zero schema or table privileges.","evidence_ids":["cmd-c7c999b813904e7d","cmd-e3da44128e02413c"]},{"id":"R4","requirement":"Committed inserts on node1 arrive on node2.","status":"satisfied","summary":"After row 1003 was committed on node1, node2 directly showed that row with the same amount, matching executed/read positions, both replication threads running, and zero lag.","evidence_ids":["cmd-ecf4c17605a641a4","cmd-c6ec16186e8049fb"]},{"id":"R5","requirement":"After a short replica disconnect, node2 catches up without losing or duplicating ledger rows.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The captured transition shows a healthy three-row baseline, both replica threads stopped, two committed primary writes while node2 remained behind, and successful recovery to five rows with five distinct IDs, the correct 39.50 total, matching position 1642, zero lag, and no replication errors.","evidence_ids":["cmd-077f8fd1aa0240c7","cmd-30fbc0d5