-cbd32d5ba7c44070, cmd-9189554066f44931, cmd-d4ca7996236c4216). MariaDB listening on port 3306 is task-related, and no new package inconsistency or failed task service was observed.","evidence_ids":["cmd-d0f38ce820e64cc0","cmd-a6943d31f3f34c40","cmd-d789f341d5b44e54","cmd-cbd32d5ba7c44070","cmd-0ebf19a04d4748b2","cmd-a8cf4c89b4004cdc","cmd-9189554066f44931","cmd-d4ca7996236c4216","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node2:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node2:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied with direct behavioral evidence. Replication was demonstrated both during normal operation and through a bounded disconnect-and-catch-up transition. The mandatory restart protocol was also completed coherently on both nodes: healthy pre-restart state, restart acknowledgement and connection loss, changed boot identities independently confirmed by lifecycle snapshots, and recovered service, data, and replication state.","limitations":["The lifecycle failed-service probe was unsupported because it checks systemd on Alpine; service health is instead supported by direct OpenRC and MariaDB checks.","Final lifecycle snapshots did not inventory /root, so retained SSH and secret files are inferred from their creation and the absence of any captured cleanup rather than independently confirmed by the final snapshot.","No explicit post-task hash was captured for node2's original export path; preservation is directly proven for node1, while node2 bootstrap used a separate /tmp copy."]}
